=== Cursor Memory Bounding Demo (pycubrid 1.6+) ===

[setup] Seeded 5000 rows into cookbook_fetch_probe

Comparing peak client memory for a full table scan of 5000 wide rows:

  fetch_size=   10  peak_memory={{MEM}} KB
  fetch_size=  100  peak_memory={{MEM}} KB
  fetch_size= 1000  peak_memory={{MEM}} KB

Peak memory ratio (largest / smallest): {{RATIO}}x

Key takeaway: smaller fetch_size caps peak client memory at the
cost of more round-trips. Choose a fetch_size that matches your
expected working set and broker latency.

--- fetch_size vs arraysize ---
  fetch_size: server page size (connection-level, set via connect())
  arraysize:  client batch size for cursor.fetchmany() (per-cursor)
  They are INDEPENDENT. fetch_size governs network/memory paging;
  arraysize governs how many rows fetchmany() returns per call.
